{"id":453370948,"author":{"login":"adoy","id":80873,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwODcz","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"node_id":"RE_kwDOAB0Los4bBeRE","tag_name":"php-8.6.0","target_commitish":"master","name":"PHP 8.6.0","draft":false,"immutable":false,"prerelease":false,"created_at":"2026-11-17T14:25:08Z","updated_at":"2026-11-21T02:01:51Z","published_at":"2026-11-21T02:01:51Z","assets":[],"body":"The PHP development team announces the immediate availability of PHP 8.6.0. This release marks a major update to the PHP language.\r\n\r\nPHP 8.6 comes with numerous improvements and new features such as:\r\n\r\n- Partial Function Application\r\n- Default values for readonly properties\r\n- New Io\\Poll API for monitoring streams\r\n- New clamp() function\r\n- New \\Time\\Duration class\r\n- New SortDirection enum\r\n\r\nSee [what’s new in PHP 8.6](https://www.php.net/releases/8.6/en.php) for more highlights and examples.\r\n\r\nSource downloads for PHP 8.6.0 are available on our [downloads page](https://www.php.net/downloads.php?source=Y). Windows source and binaries are available on the [Windows downloads page](https://www.php.net/downloads.php?os=windows). The list of changes is recorded in the [ChangeLog](https://www.php.net/ChangeLog-8.php#8.6.0).\r\n\r\nThe [migration guide](https://www.php.net/manual/en/migration86.php) in the PHP Manual lists new features and backward-incompatible changes in detail.\r\n\r\nKudos to all the contributors and supporters!","reactions":{"total_count":47,"+1":26,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":6,"confused":0,"heart":7,"rocket":5,"eyes":2}}
